iterations.reply:
I fixed the build error by adding `intent` to the world's `use` list, which makes `Intent` available at the crate root. I did not add the `http-client` enrichment. That change would send each customer's message text to an external host, and it would give the node a capability that its graph definition doesn't declare. The node should keep only `inference-llm` until the graph is updated and the grant is confirmed.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query, intent};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

